# hd6309.silicon - where SILICON corrects The 6309 Book's Appendix A cycles.
#
# ⭐ hd6309.tab is the book's record and stays so; this is the list of places
# it is wrong, and mk6309tab.py applies it when it writes hd6309ops.h - so the
# core runs on silicon's figure and the book's is still there to read.  The
# authority is hoglet67's 6809Decoder (instr_table_6309, validated against
# logic-analyser captures of real HD6309s); oracle/checkcyc.py fetches it and
# requires the corrected table to agree with it EXACTLY.
#
#   page op em nm   reason
#
# ⭐ THE PREFIXED INHERENT OPS, all of them: the book gives 2/1 for NEGD..CLRD
# and 2/2 for COME..CLRF, which a two-byte instruction cannot take - each byte
# is a bus cycle.  The book dropped the prefix's cycle for the whole group.
1 40 3 2   NEGD - the prefix's cycle
1 43 3 2   COMD
1 44 3 2   LSRD
1 46 3 2   RORD
1 47 3 2   ASRD
1 48 3 2   ASLD
1 49 3 2   ROLD
1 4A 3 2   DECD
1 4C 3 2   INCD
1 4D 3 2   TSTD
1 4F 3 2   CLRD
1 5F 3 2   CLRW - the book's native 1 is the same slip
2 43 3 2   COME
2 4A 3 2   DECE
2 4C 3 2   INCE
2 4D 3 2   TSTE
2 4F 3 2   CLRE
2 53 3 2   COMF
2 5A 3 2   DECF
2 5C 3 2   INCF
2 5D 3 2   TSTF
2 5F 3 2   CLRF
# ⭐ TIM never writes, so it is the SHORTEST of the four logical-memory ops,
# not the longest - the book's 6 and 7+ are OCR or transcription.
0 0B 4 4   TIM direct
0 6B 5 5   TIM indexed (base, before the postbyte)
0 65 7 7   EIM indexed: the book's 6+ is one short of OIM and AIM's 7+
0 14 4 4   SEXW
0 1A 3 3   ORCC: no native saving
0 13 4 3   SYNC: the minimum, which native mode shortens by one
